+# Replace faker with deterministic test fixtures
+
+The premise was verified before editing: a repository-wide `rg` search of Go and
+BUILD files found only these two test imports and their two BUILD references.
+This change leaves `github.com/go-faker/faker/v4` with no first-party users.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Explicit textproto fixtures populate all fields of the five proto types used
+  by the tests and benchmarks, including nested and repeated messages. Descriptor
+  reflection requires every field to be populated, so newly added fields cannot
+  silently lose coverage. Empty messages are also included in size checks and
+  benchmark fixtures. Benchmark input selection is deterministic.
+- An explicit primary-DB invocation fixture gives every compared field a nonzero
+  value, using distinct numeric and string values. The existing reflection-based
+  comparison remains; a nonzero assertion also catches incomplete fixture updates.
+  UUID and tag conversion expectations are explicit.
+- Removed both faker BUILD dependencies; added textproto and reflection packages
+  from the already-used protobuf module. Existing fallback, unknown-field, and
+  external VT message checks remain.
+
+## Measurements
+
+Measured over the two test files and their BUILD files with the same script for
+baseline (commit `770b88bc89c0b20059d42a237e8c7923ff5b7215`) and working tree (`REV=HEAD python /tmp/faker-metrics.py` and
+`python /tmp/faker-metrics.py`, before committing). Script reproduced below.
+
+| Metric | Before | After |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Test targets | 2 | 2 |
+| Direct test dependency edges | 14 | 14 |
+| Unique direct external labels | 7 | 8 |
+| Unique direct external repositories/modules | 4 | 3 |
+| Faker BUILD edges | 2 | 0 |
+| Faker Go imports | 2 | 0 |
+| LOC across scoped files | 629 | 729 |
+
+The extra package labels belong to protobuf, an existing dependency. One test-only
+module becomes removable; no production binary-size improvement is claimed.
+Benchmark timings should not be compared directly with the old 30 randomly filled
+samples: the new corpus contains one empty and one fully populated message per type.
+
+```python
+import os,re,subprocess
+from pathlib import Path
+files=['server/util/proto/proto_test.go','server/util/proto/BUILD','server/util/clickhouse/schema/schema_test.go','server/util/clickhouse/schema/BUILD']
+rev=os.getenv('REV')
+texts=[subprocess.check_output(['git','show',rev+':'+f],text=True) if rev else Path(f).read_text() for f in files]
+labels=[v for i,t in enumerate(texts) if files[i].endswith('/BUILD') for v in re.findall(r'"([:@/][^"\n]+)"',t)]
+print('LOC:',sum(len(t.splitlines()) for t in texts))
+print('test targets:',sum(t.count('go_test(') for t in texts))
+# Only deps of the test rules, not imports, visibility, or libraries.
+deps=[v for i,t in enumerate(texts) if files[i].endswith('/BUILD') for v in re.findall(r'"([:@/][^"\n]+)"',t.split('go_test(')[1].split('deps = [')[1].split(']')[0])]
+print('test direct dependency edges:',len(deps))
+print('unique test external labels:',len(set(v for v in deps if v.startswith('@'))))
+print('unique test external repos:',len(set(v.split('//')[0] for v in deps if v.startswith('@'))))
+print('faker BUILD edges:',sum('go_faker' in v for v in deps))
+print('faker Go imports:',sum(t.count('"github.com/go-faker/faker/v4"') for t in texts))
+```
+
+## Unused module evidence
+
+```sh
+git grep -n -E 'github.com/go-faker/faker/v4|com_github_go_faker_faker_v4' HEAD -- '*.go' '**/BUILD' '**/BUILD.bazel'
+git grep -n -E 'github.com/go-faker/faker/v4|com_github_go_faker_faker_v4' -- '*.go' '**/BUILD' '**/BUILD.bazel'
+```
+
+Baseline: four matches (the two imports and two dependency edges). Working tree:
+zero matches (exit 1). `rg -n 'go-faker' go.mod` still finds version
+`v4.0.0-beta.3`. Shared dependency manifests and lockfiles were left unchanged for
+the separate serialized dependency-removal PR. A full-repository search,
+`rg -n 'go-faker|com_github_go_faker' --glob '!result.md'`, finds only these shared
+manifests: `go.mod`, `go.sum`, and `deps/go_deps.MODULE.bazel`.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(//..., set(//server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test), 1)'`
+  failed during repository loading: the unrelated `default_execution_image` Docker
+  repository build exceeded its rule timeout. Log: `/tmp/faker-rdeps.log`.
+- `bazel query 'labels(deps, set(//server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test))'`
+  passed. It returns 13 unique direct dependency labels, with no faker label.
+  Log: `/tmp/faker-after-deps.log`.
+- Initial `bazel test //server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test`
+  built and ran the tests, whose logs show PASS, but exited 1 due to the schema
+  test's `embedlit` static-analysis check. Applied its recommended promoted-field
+  fixture syntax. Log: `/tmp/faker-test.log` (31-minute cold build).
+
+- `bazel query --notool_deps --noimplicit_deps 'rdeps(//..., set(//server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test), 1)'`
+  failed (exit 7) while downloading the unrelated macOS Bazel 9.2.0 repository:
+  `No space left on device`. Log: `/tmp/faker-rdeps-explicit.log`.
+- Final `bazel test //server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test`
+  passed (exit 0): **2 tests pass**, proto cached and schema rerun; static analysis
+  passed. Warm rebuild critical path: 8.90 seconds (reported elapsed time includes
+  waiting for the query). Log: `/tmp/faker-test-final.log`.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(set(//server/util/proto:all //server/util/clickhouse/schema:all), set(//server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test), 1)'`
+  passed (exit 0), returning only the two changed tests. Log:
+  `/tmp/faker-rdeps-scoped.log`.
+- `bazel query 'labels(tests, kind(test_suite, //...)) intersect set(//server/util/proto:proto_test //server/util/clickhouse/schema:schema_test)'`
+  passed (exit 0), returning no test-suite users. Log: `/tmp/faker-suite-users.log`.
+- `rg -n 'proto:proto_test|schema:schema_test' --glob BUILD --glob BUILD.bazel`
+  finds no explicit references to these test labels anywhere in first-party
+  BUILD files.
+
+The full-universe reverse-dependency query could not complete because of the
+unrelated repository setup failures above. The scoped query, suite-user query,
+and reference search found no additional direct reverse dependencies to test.
+
+`gofmt` applied to both test files; `git diff --check` passed.
+Long Bazel commands ran under `nohup`, with logs in `/tmp/faker-*.log` and polling.
+
+## Scope and omissions
+
+Only the four authorized source/BUILD files and this explicitly requested report
+were changed. No dependency manifest changes, push, or PR. No broad build of `//...`.
